AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Keys
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands >Keys< Exit codes  Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Moving around
 3 Streams       │   Menu on the left, page on the right. Arrows move, Enter goes in, Esc comes back.
 4 Recognitions  │   The menu is the sidebar; Help, Streams, Recognitions, and Account have a tab bar above their page.
 5 Account       │   On a choice ‹ like this ›, ←/→ change it and ← on its first option goes back. While you type in a
 6 Settings      │   field, letters and digits go into it: esc leaves the field, ctrl+u clears it. What a page can do is
*7 Help          >   on its buttons: tab (or ↓ from the end of the page) reaches them, ←/→ move between them, enter
                 │   presses one. A letter on a button, such as (o), presses it from anywhere on the page. A key works
                 │   only where it is listed; any other key says it does nothing. Opening a page never starts typing:
                 │   its field is selected, a letter starts typing in it, enter edits it, and 1-7 jump to a section
                 │   except while you type. Settings of audd save right away (u undoes the last change). Spending more
                 │   than one request, removing, signing out, or replacing the token asks in a dialog: enter presses the
                 │   focused button (the action after a plan, Cancel otherwise), y confirms, n or esc cancels; in a
                 │   dialog y confirms instead of copying the command.
                 │ 
                 │   ↑/↓            move in the menu, a list, or a form
                 │   → or enter     go in: open the section, the page, the selected item
                 │   ← or esc       come back one level (in typed text ← moves the cursor)
                 │   ←/→            on a tab bar: switch tabs; on a choice: change it
                 │   ↑              from the top of a page: back to its tab bar
                 │   [ ]            previous or next tab, from anywhere in the section outside text fields
                 │ 
                 │ Everywhere
                 │   1-7            jump to a section (not while typing in a text field)
                 │   ctrl+k or :    run any command; ctrl+k again closes it
                 │   y              copy the command shown at the bottom (in a dialog: confirm)
                 │   ?              keys for this screen
                 │   F1             help
                 │   q              quit; not while typing, and it asks while a command runs
                 │   ctrl+c         quit, also while typing (it asks while a command runs)
                 │   ctrl+u         clear the field being typed in
                 │   click, wheel   select or press; scroll
                 │ 
 ctrl+k commands │ Letters on buttons
 ? keys  q quit  │ ↓ 66 more lines below

←/→ tabs  ↓ open  esc back  ? keys
ctrl+k runs any audd command